# The kernel's review (roadmap os-server.md P15), finding 7: a thread that lost its last capability while it ran ends at
# its call's next window, never off the CPU while its control block's
# memory is given out again (before: the scheduler ran a control block
# written through a segment). tests/programs/
# additions.asm, TEST_RV_DEAD; Bochs, whose timing the races need.
program: additions
define: TEST_CAPS
define: TEST_RV_DEAD
emulators: bochs
match: contains
timeout: 60
---
additions: R's control block written through a segment
additions: still here
additions: done
